        "answer": "Martin Axenrot recorded Opeth's Pale Communion (2014) using the same custom hand-made DW kit with maple/gum shells he had established since Watershed and carried through Heritage (2011): twin 22\"x18\" bass drums, 10\" and 12\" rack toms, 14\" and 16\" floor toms. He paired the DW kit with SABIAN HHX/AAX cymbals (15\" HHX Groove Hats, 18\" HHX Evolution O-Zone Crash, 21\" HHX Legacy Ride, 20\" HHX Chinese, 12\" HHX Splash, 10\" AAX Splash) and a set of twin pedals whose specific hardware brand is unverified. Tracked at Fascination Street Studios in Örebro, Sweden, produced by Mikael Åkerfeldt and mixed by Steven Wilson."
