        "answer": "Opeth moved from Roadrunner Records to Nuclear Blast for Sorceress after their Roadrunner contract concluded. Nuclear Blast was one of the world's leading metal labels by 2016, with distribution and promotional infrastructure that better served Opeth's commercial ambitions in the prog-rock era. The label move did not change the creative approach — Sorceress was still produced by Mikael Åkerfeldt at Fascination Street Studios in Örebro, with the same custom hand-made DW kit and SABIAN HHX/AAX cymbal setup as Heritage and Pale Communion. The #1 chart debuts in Sweden and Norway validated the move commercially."
